## Summary

Consistency audit of main at ad71839, checking the whole codebase against AGENTS.md, docs/ and its own idioms.

**What I checked.** Mechanical style rules (gofmt, `interface{}`, `make()`, lowercase log and error messages, comments in Go and JS, long flags with double dashes in docs). Also whether file paths and code names cited in docs exist, user-facing wording in `web/`, and the tools' output messages. The codebase was already clean on nearly all of it.

**What changed.**
- **Web UI failure messages** now share one form, "Couldn’t …" with a curly apostrophe, instead of mixing "Could not …", "Failed to load …" and a straight-apostrophe copy. Eight messages in `web/common/personcard.js`, `web/team/edit.js`, `web/home/adminpage.js`, `web/common/admin.js`, `web/who/pages/admin.js` and `web/who/pages/invites.js`. A reviewer caught that the first pass dropped the space after the colon in five; fixed.
- **`docs/storage.md`:** `Store.Tick` is in `internal/store/queue.go`, not `store.go`; the sentence names both files.
- **`tools/sheets` (`drop`):** its `dry run:` message now matches the six other `reporting only, pass --apply …` messages in that tool. A reviewer asked to revert this; I declined because the tool was inconsistent with itself.

**Deliberately left alone.** The Claude prompts' British "summarise" (changing prompts could force paid re-extraction). The server's lowercase "could not …" error text (a different register from client toasts). CSS comments (the prevailing idiom). The tools using `log` while the server uses `slog`. Button label capitalization (Title Case vs sentence case, a design choice).

**Merge of main.** `git merge --no-ff --no-commit main` reported "Already up to date", so nothing was merged and no conflicts arose. `go vet ./...` was run after.

